.TH SPT 1 spt\-VERSION
.SH NAME
spt \- simple pomodoro timer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spt
.RB [ \-a
.IR audiofile ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR notifyext ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR notifycmd ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR tracker ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spt
is a simple timer that uses pomodoro technique with desktop notification to
double your efficiency.
.B spt
accepts the following control signals:
.P
.RS
.B SIGUSR1
\- show remaining time, state
.br
.B SIGUSR2
\- play/pause the timer, work soundtrack, and work-time tracking
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " audiofile"
Play
.I audiofile
using mplayer during work intervals only.
The file loops until the interval ends and restarts at the next work interval.
Playback pauses with the timer and stops before a break or on SIGINT,
SIGTERM, or SIGHUP.
The argument is a filename, not a shell command.
.TP
.BI \-e " notifyext"
Execute
.I notifyext
for every notification, including work starts, break starts, and SIGUSR1
status requests. Pass an empty string to disable the configured command.
.TP
.BI \-n " notifycmd"
Execute
.I notifycmd
if not compiled with
.IR "-DNOTIFY".
.TP
.BI \-t " tracker"
Use the standalone tracker executable (default: timetrack, found in PATH).
The argument may be an executable name or a full path; it is not a shell
command. An empty string disables tracking.
The executable may be installed anywhere. spt calls its existing morning,
break, resume and closing commands. The tracker must allow closing during a
break and is installed separately from spt.
.TP
.BI \-v
Prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH TIMER
4 pomodoro timer (
.B 25 min.
) with subsequent rests in between (
.B 5 min.
) and followed by a long rest (
.B 15 min.
) in an infinite loop.
Each entry in config.h contains a duration in seconds, a work flag
(1 for work, 0 for break), and a notification message.
.SH TIME TRACKING
The first work period starts a session with morning. Breaks and manual work
pauses use break; returning to work uses resume. Exiting spt uses closing
once tracking has started. Status requests, initial breaks and resuming a
scheduled break do not change tracking.
.PP
On shutdown during work, a break or a pause, spt calls closing once. Closing
a break records departure without restarting work or counting any break
time. The standalone tracker must support this sequence.
.PP
A helper inside spt closes the session if the main timer disappears,
including after SIGKILL, provided that helper survives. Tracker commands
exit after each update. A failed command stops the timer with an error.
.PP
Read statistics directly through the standalone tracker. Start with a closed
session, and avoid concurrent manual changes or timers for the same session.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use system notify_send and play a music without libnotify:
.IP
spt -e 'aplay alarm.wav' -n 'notify-send'
.PP
Play a work soundtrack and disable the extra notification command:
.IP
spt -a "$CONCENTRATION_SOUNDTRACK" -e '' -n 'notify-send'
.PP
Use a standalone tracker installed at another path:
.IP
spt -t "$HOME/.local/bin/timetrack.py" -a "$CONCENTRATION_SOUNDTRACK" -e ''
